# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your real keys.
# .env.local is gitignored (matches the *.local pattern) — never commit real keys.
#
# --- Browser keys (used by the React app, safe to expose) ---

# Track-Asia (https://account.track-asia.com) — Vietnamese map platform built on
# OpenStreetMap data. Free tier: 50,000 geocode + 1,000,000 tile requests/day.
# Provides place search, coordinates, reverse geocoding, routing and vector tiles.
# Does NOT provide ratings, opening hours or photos — the app falls back to its
# curated seed dataset for those.
VITE_TRACK_ASIA_API_KEY=

# Supabase project (supabase.com dashboard → Project Settings → API)
# The anon key is safe to expose — actual access is controlled by Row Level Security policies.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Supabase Edge Function secrets (NEVER put these in this file / never prefix VITE_) ---
# Set these on the Supabase project instead, via:
#   supabase secrets set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=... GOOGLE_PLACES_SERVER_KEY=... YOUTUBE_API_KEY=... GOOGLE_CUSTOM_SEARCH_KEY=... GOOGLE_CUSTOM_SEARCH_CX=...
# They're listed here only as documentation of what each one is for:
#
# GOOGLE_PLACES_SERVER_KEY  — same Google Cloud project as above, a SEPARATE key restricted by
#                             IP instead of HTTP referrer, used by the verify-place Edge Function.
#                             Also used locally (not as a Supabase secret) by
#                             scripts/crawl-real-places.js — run as
#                             GOOGLE_PLACES_SERVER_KEY=... node scripts/crawl-real-places.js
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY         — console.anthropic.com → API Keys. Used by the detect-place and
#                             parse-trip-request Edge Functions.
# YOUTUBE_API_KEY           — same Google Cloud project → enable "YouTube Data API v3". Used by
#                             the youtube-shorts Edge Function (TikTok/IG/FB have no public search
#                             API, so only YouTube can be automated this way). Also used locally by
#                             scripts/crawl-youtube-captions.js — run as
#                             YOUTUBE_API_KEY=... node scripts/crawl-youtube-captions.js
# GOOGLE_CUSTOM_SEARCH_KEY,
# GOOGLE_CUSTOM_SEARCH_CX   — Google Custom Search JSON API + a Programmable Search Engine
#                             ("Search the entire web") — lets the tiktok-web-search Edge Function
#                             find real, Google-indexed TikTok video pages. Only works well for
#                             TikTok — Facebook/Instagram posts are barely indexed by Google.
#                             Also used by search-hotel-listings to find a hotel's real Agoda/
#                             Traveloka listing page (there's no public booking API for either —
#                             this is a "find the real page" lookup, not a price/inventory feed).
# VNPAY_TMN_CODE,
# VNPAY_HASH_SECRET         — Sandbox merchant credentials from https://sandbox.vnpayment.vn/devreg/
#                             (register a free sandbox merchant account — no real business needed).
#                             Used by vnpay-create-payment/vnpay-return to sign payment requests for
#                             the hotel booking flow. Without these, booking falls back to a clearly
#                             labeled demo confirmation instead of a real payment.
# APP_URL                   — your deployed frontend origin (e.g. https://yourdomain.com), used by
#                             vnpay-return to redirect the browser back after payment. Defaults to
#                             http://localhost:5173 if unset — note VNPay's sandbox can't redirect to
#                             localhost from a real browser session, only works when APP_URL is a
#                             publicly reachable URL (e.g. via a tunnel, or your deployed site).
